From: Philippe Simons <simons.philippe@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8250: A650 overclock OPPs to 750 MHz, voltage raised with the clock

Add GPU OPPs above the stock 587 MHz: 650 and 670 MHz at NOM_L1 (670
opened to speed bin 0, the base SD865), 700 MHz at TURBO, 725 and
750 MHz at TURBO_L1. Each carries the 587 MHz DDR vote of the stock
bus table.

The previous ladder ran 650, 700, 750 and 800 MHz all at NOM_L1 --
upstream's corner for 670 MHz on bins 1 and 3 only -- so every step
above 670 was undervolted. 800 MHz is dropped: it was measured adding
almost nothing over 750 MHz on an A650 (82 C, near the 85 C passive
trip, fan already at full speed).

These steps are reachable by the devfreq governor, not only by a
manual clock.
---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250.dtsi
index 54269f574..d5354e25e 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250.dtsi
@@ -2976,10 +2976,38 @@ gpu_zap_shader: zap-shader {
 			gpu_opp_table: opp-table {
 				compatible = "operating-points-v2";
 
+				opp-750000000 {
+					opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <750000000>;
+					opp-level = <RPMH_REGULATOR_LEVEL_TURBO_L1>;
+					opp-supported-hw = <0xb>;
+					opp-peak-kBps = <8171875>;
+				};
+
+				opp-725000000 {
+					opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <725000000>;
+					opp-level = <RPMH_REGULATOR_LEVEL_TURBO_L1>;
+					opp-supported-hw = <0xb>;
+					opp-peak-kBps = <8171875>;
+				};
+
+				opp-700000000 {
+					opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <700000000>;
+					opp-level = <RPMH_REGULATOR_LEVEL_TURBO>;
+					opp-supported-hw = <0xb>;
+					opp-peak-kBps = <8171875>;
+				};
+
 				opp-670000000 {
 					opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <670000000>;
 					opp-level = <RPMH_REGULATOR_LEVEL_NOM_L1>;
-					opp-supported-hw = <0xa>;
+					opp-supported-hw = <0xb>;
+					opp-peak-kBps = <8171875>;
+				};
+
+				opp-650000000 {
+					opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <650000000>;
+					opp-level = <RPMH_REGULATOR_LEVEL_NOM_L1>;
+					opp-supported-hw = <0xb>;
 					opp-peak-kBps = <8171875>;
 				};
 
